From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:25:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DWPose bbox detector on GPU: TorchScript instead of ONNX

The pose estimator was already TorchScript and ran on the GPU; the
bounding-box detector was yolox_l.onnx, which goes through onnxruntime.
Its CUDA provider will not load against torch 2.8.0+cu128, so
comfyui_controlnet_aux clears AUX_ORT_PROVIDERS and runs the detector on
CPU - once per frame, twice per clip, for the face pass and the
body/hands pass.

Measured on a 4-second swap: 45s GPU busy against 14m20s idle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YKsc8cx34uFtw34kMSZZE9
---
 workflows/wan_animate.json | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/workflows/wan_animate.json b/workflows/wan_animate.json
index 44afe1c..22f966e 100644
--- a/workflows/wan_animate.json
+++ b/workflows/wan_animate.json
@@ -194,7 +194,7 @@
         "158",
         0
       ],
-      "bbox_detector": "yolox_l.onnx",
+      "bbox_detector": "yolox_l.torchscript.pt",
       "pose_estimator": "dw-ll_ucoco_384_bs5.torchscript.pt",
       "scale_stick_for_xinsr_cn": "disable",
       "image": [
@@ -218,7 +218,7 @@
         "158",
         0
       ],
-      "bbox_detector": "yolox_l.onnx",
